note A three page application. This is the example from the original Shark
note concept document, written against the Edition 2026 grammar.

page Home
  in a column spaced 12
    show text Welcome to Shark
    show button Get Started to page Level One

page Level One
  in a column spaced 12
    show text You have reached the first level
    show button Go to the final level to page Level Two
    show button Back to page Home

page Level Two
  in a column spaced 12
    show text You have reached the second level
    show button Return to page Home

note ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
note The same three pages written with explicit event handlers instead of the
note `to page` shorthand. Both forms produce identical SIR.

page Home Long Form
  show text Welcome to Shark
  show button Get Started named start

  when start is pressed
    open page Level One
